ok    Disk space          120 GB free on the drive that holds Puddle's data (/home/dev/.local/share/puddle)
FAIL  Data folder path    /home/dev/.local is writable by the group and not sticky, so msb will not open Puddle's data below it
      fix:  msb opens its catalog only below folders where other accounts cannot rename entries,
            so every sandbox start fails until the write permission is gone. A user created with
            a private group and umask 0002 (the Ubuntu default) often leaves ~/.local at 0775.
            Run:
              chmod g-w /home/dev/.local
      from: /home/dev/.local mode 0775
ok    Disk encryption     data drive encrypted (BitLocker); swap /dev/dm-1 encrypted (BitLocker)
ok    SSH agent           the agent on /run/user/1000/agent.sock holds 1 key (ed25519: 1)
ok    Azure CLI (az)      version 2.64.0
ok    Credential store    the operating system's credential store: a test write and delete worked

1 problem to fix before Puddle can run sandboxes. (1.2 s)

